{
  "id": "014",
  "title": "Hostage Heart",
  "subtitle": "They took me from a Manhattan parking garage on a Wednesday night. The man who carried me to the South of France told me my husband had refused to negotiate.",
  "penName": "Sasha Lake",
  "genre": "darkMafia",
  "hook": "They took me from the parking garage of my Manhattan office on a Wednesday night. The man who carried me out had bone-cold hands and apologized through a black silk scarf. They drove me to a stone house in the South of France with a courtyard full of olive trees and a man named Reign who was not the one I had been taken to leverage. He looked at me like I was a math error in his quarterly report. He offered me coffee. He told me my husband had refused to negotiate. He told me he was sorry.",
